I'm encountering an issue where CVX sometimes solves a problem successfully, and sometimes it fails with the error:
"错误使用 cvx/sum (line 56)
Disciplined convex programming error:
 Illegal addition encountered (e.g., {convex} + {concave})."

I'm confident that the problem is convex. The issue arises when summing results from different loops. Here's my input parameters and CVX optimization problem.

**Input Parameters:**
```matlab
N = 5;  % array number of BS
Nr = 6;
M = 10; % array number of STAR-RIS
M1 = M/2;
K = 2;  % number of users
SNR_dB = 10; % dBW
cof_L = 0.8; % coefficient of loop interference
cof_S = 0.8; % coefficient of self interference
cof = [cof_S; 1]; % select coefficient 21 dimension
N0 = 10^((-174-30) / 10); % -174dBm
B = 10^7; % 10MHz
down_maxpower_all = 20;
up_maxpower_all = 1;
noise_maxpower_original = 10^((-80-30) / 10); % -80dBm
power_max_dBm = 10;
num_loop = 100;
num_iterative = 10;
```

**CVX Optimization Problem:**
```matlab
function [F_opt, flag] = Generate_ESMS_recv_beamforming(cof, cof_L, N, Nr, M, K, H_IB, H_BI, H_BB, H_IU, H_UI, H_IE, W_ini, F_ini, Phi_ini, u_up_ini, u_dwn_ini, noise_maxpower, down_maxpower, up_maxpower)
    cvx_begin quiet
    variable F(K, Nr) complex
    expressions up_r(K);

    for i = 1:1:K
        up_USER_ch(:, i) = u_up_ini(i) * H_IB * diag(sum(H_UI, 1)) * Phi_ini(i, :)';
        up_USER_poly(:, :, i) = up_maxpower * up_USER_ch(:, i) * up_USER_ch(:, i)';
        real_part_ch(:, i) = u_up_ini(i) * H_IB * diag(H_UI(i, :)) * Phi_ini(i, :)';
        real_part_ini(i) = 2 * real(sqrt(up_maxpower) * F_ini(i, :) * real_part_ch(:, i));
        upLI_ch(:, i) = u_up_ini(i) * H_BB' * sum(W_ini, 2);
        upLI_poly(:, :, i) = upLI_ch(:, i) * upLI_ch(:, i)';
        upLI_ini(i) = F_ini(i, :) * upLI_poly(:, :, i) * F_ini(i, :)';
        upSI_ch(:, i) = u_up_ini(i) * H_IB * H_BI * sum(W_ini, 2);
        upSI_poly(:, :, i) = upSI_ch(:, i) * upSI_ch(:, i)';
        upSI_ini(i) = F_ini(i, :) * upSI_poly(:, :, i) * F_ini(i, :)';
        nois_poly(i) = noise_maxpower * u_up_ini(i) * u_up_ini(i);
        nois_ini(i) = F_ini(i, :) * nois_poly(i) * F_ini(i, :)';
        up_e_poly(:, :, i) = up_USER_poly(:, :, i) + upLI_poly(:, :, i) + upSI_poly(:, :, i) + nois_poly(i);
        aux_var(i) = 1 / (up_USER_ini(i) - real_part_ini(i) + upLI_ini(i) + upSI_ini(i) + nois_ini(i) + 1);
        final_matrix(:, :, i) = aux_var(i) * up_e_poly(:, :, i);
        A_matrix(:, :, i) = 0.5 * (final_matrix(:, :, i) + final_matrix(:, :, i)');
        real_part(:, i) = sqrt(up_maxpower) * real_part_ch(:, i) * aux_var(i);
        up_r(i) = -F(i, :) * A_matrix(:, :, i) * F(i, :)' + 2 * real(F(i, :) * real_part(:, i));
    end
    maximize sum(up_r)
    pow_pos(norm(F, 'fro'), 2) <= 1;
    cvx_end
    if cvx_status(1) == 'S' || cvx_status(3) == 'a'
        flag = 1;
        F_opt = F;
    else
        flag = 0;
        F_opt = ones(K, Nr);
    end
end
```

I don't know what's wrong with my code. Can someone help find out? Thanks!

**Error Message:**
