The reason I didn't include the constraint \(\sum \tau = 1\) was that I thought it should be iterated by a one-dimensional search method, considering it as a new AO variable. I tried adding this constraint to the optimization problem, but the optimal value is still zero. Here's my program:

```matlab
function [W, flag] = Generate_TS_W(N, M, K, H, G, W_ini, Fi_ini_TS, t_ini, noise_maxpower, trans_maxpower)
    cvx_begin
    variable W(N, K) complex
    variable tau(K)
    expressions POLY_TS(K);
    Phi = Fi_ini_TS;
    k = 1:K;
    u = K:-1:1;
    for i = 1:length(k)
        if k(i) == 1 && u(i) == 1
            a(k(i)) = 0.5;
            H_eqvi(k(i), :) = H(:, k(i))' + Fi_ini_TS(k(i), :) * G(:, :, k(i));
            H_eqvi(u(i), :) = H(:, u(i))' + Fi_ini_TS(u(i), :) * G(:, :, u(i));
            H_eqv(k(i), :) = H(:, k(i))' + Phi(k(i), :) * G(:, :, k(i));
            H_eqv(u(i), :) = H(:, u(i))' + Phi(u(i), :) * G(:, :, u(i));
            B_g1(k(i)) = H_eqvi(k(i), :) * W_ini(:, k(i));
            B_g2(k(i)) = H_eqvi(k(i), :) * W_ini(:, u(i));
            B_g3(k(i)) = H_eqvi(u(i), :) * W_ini(:, k(i));
            B_g4(k(i)) = H_eqvi(u(i), :) * W_ini(:, u(i));
            B_1(k(i)) = H_eqv(k(i), :) * W(:, k(i));
            B_2(k(i)) = H_eqv(k(i), :) * W(:, u(i));
            B_3(k(i)) = H_eqv(u(i), :) * W(:, k(i));
            B_4(k(i)) = H_eqv(u(i), :) * W(:, u(i));
            POLY_1(k(i)) = 2 / noise_maxpower * real(B_1(k(i))' * B_g1(k(i)));
            c(k(i)) = (abs(B_g1(k(i)))^2) / (noise_maxpower * (noise_maxpower + abs(B_g1(k(i)))^2));
            POLY_2(k(i)) = c(k(i)) * (abs(B_1(k(i)))^2 + noise_maxpower);
            f(k(i)) = 1 / (noise_maxpower + abs(B_g3(k(i)))^2);
            POLY_3(k(i)) = f(k(i)) * abs(B_3(k(i)))^2;
            POLY_TS(k(i)) = a .* tau(k(i)) * (POLY_1(k(i)) - POLY_2(k(i)) - POLY_3(k(i)));
        end
    end
    maximize sum(POLY_TS)
    subject to
        for i = 1:length(k)
            if k(i) == 1 && u(i) == 1
                norm(W, 'fro')^2 <= trans_maxpower;
                sum(tau) == 1;
            end
        end
    cvx_end
    if cvx_status(1) == 'S' || cvx_status(3) == 'a'
        flag = 1;
    else
        flag = 0;
    end
end
```

**Input Data:**
```matlab
N = 3; M = 6; K = 2; noise_maxpower = 1; trans_maxpower = 100;
b = 2 * pi; a = 0;
Fi_temp = (b - a) .* rand(2, M) + sqrt(-1) * (b - a) .* rand(2, M);
Fi_amp = rand(2, M);
Fi_ini_TS = Fi_amp .* exp(1j * angle(Fi_temp));
W_ini = randn(N, K) * sqrt(trans_maxpower / (N * K));
H = rand(N, K);
G = rand(M, N, K);
```

Hello everyone, I am facing an issue where the problem occurs in the second iteration. I have checked the details in the first iteration, and the output is close to the desired result, but it stops in the second and third iterations.

What I want to solve is as follows:
γl+1 is equal to gama1_inv

